WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.820
Healthcare.

00:00:07.839 --> 00:00:11.560
Education.

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:12.580
Water.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:13.759
Nutrition.

00:00:13.779 --> 00:00:16.800
There are so many pockets of the world that still are in

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:19.070
extreme poverty.

00:00:19.089 --> 00:00:22.039
A billion people living on $1.25 is wrong!

00:00:22.059 --> 00:00:23.059
It's just wrong!

00:00:23.059 --> 00:00:25.059
And we've got to do something about it.

00:00:25.059 --> 00:00:28.719
All of the things that lead to poverty alleviation come from

00:00:28.739 --> 00:00:29.989
economic growth.

00:00:30.009 --> 00:00:33.809
And we believe the entrepreneurs in these economies are the

00:00:33.829 --> 00:00:34.829
engines of growth.

00:00:34.829 --> 00:00:37.889
We know that there are people out there that can make this

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:38.909
world a better place.

00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:40.709
And we want to get behind them!

00:00:40.729 --> 00:00:43.749
Thanks to a generous gift from Bob and Dottie King, Stanford

00:00:43.769 --> 00:00:47.029
University is launching a bold new initiative.

00:00:47.049 --> 00:00:49.820
I think what the gift allows us to do is it allows us to

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:52.809
think in much bigger terms about what it is that we could

00:00:52.809 --> 00:00:53.809
do.

00:00:53.809 --> 00:00:56.589
We are going to create an Institute housed in the greater

00:00:56.609 --> 00:00:58.799
School of Business to bring our knowledge about

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:02.339
entrepreneurship to entrepreneurs who are trying to make a

00:01:02.359 --> 00:01:03.609
better life.

00:01:03.629 --> 00:01:06.439
It's called the Stanford Institute for Innovation in

00:01:06.459 --> 00:01:08.519
Developing Economies.

00:01:08.539 --> 00:01:10.280
The Institute has a long name.

00:01:10.299 --> 00:01:13.620
But we nicknamed it SEED.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.459
SEED signifies possibilities.

00:01:15.479 --> 00:01:18.629
Something small that has the potential to grow.

00:01:18.649 --> 00:01:20.420
It means "hope".

00:01:20.439 --> 00:01:25.519
SEED is going to include three components: research,

00:01:25.539 --> 00:01:29.159
education and dissemination, and what we're calling an "on

00:01:29.179 --> 00:01:30.769
the ground" component.

00:01:30.789 --> 00:01:34.030
Each part of the Institute reinforces and supports the

00:01:34.049 --> 00:01:35.049
others.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:39.219
We will conduct research on how to develop management skills

00:01:39.239 --> 00:01:42.209
and create an entrepreneurial spirit.

00:01:42.229 --> 00:01:45.179
In the education and dissemination part of the Institute, we

00:01:45.199 --> 00:01:48.480
will develop courses for our students, courses for

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:52.049
entrepreneurs from developing economies, and we will take

00:01:52.069 --> 00:01:54.819
the knowledge that we have created in the research arm of

00:01:54.839 --> 00:01:59.230
the Institute and disseminate it very broadly using the web

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.250
and information technology.

00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:04.950
We also recognize the need of collaboration with on-the-

00:02:04.969 --> 00:02:07.799
ground people working with local groups to make things

00:02:07.819 --> 00:02:08.819
happen.

00:02:08.819 --> 00:02:10.929
Engineering students, medical students, business students

00:02:10.949 --> 00:02:14.849
coming together to produce new goods and services that don't

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.289
exist now.

00:02:16.310 --> 00:02:20.429
And then we're going to take existing entities from small

00:02:20.449 --> 00:02:23.079
size to much greater size.

00:02:23.099 --> 00:02:25.289
Stanford is a creature of Silicon Valley.

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:28.649
And Silicon Valley is a creature of Stanford.

00:02:28.669 --> 00:02:32.749
And what SEED is going to be able to do, which no one else

00:02:32.769 --> 00:02:37.829
has ever done, is to bring all of that genetic code, all of

00:02:37.849 --> 00:02:41.669
that secret sauce, to the places around the world that can

00:02:41.689 --> 00:02:43.649
benefit from it most.

00:02:43.669 --> 00:02:47.019
It's not just going to be a think tank; it's going to be

00:02:47.019 --> 00:02:49.299
results that are going to change people's lives.

00:02:49.319 --> 00:02:51.929
This is one of the largest gifts in Stanford's history.

00:02:51.929 --> 00:02:54.269
This is a very exciting opportunity.

00:02:54.289 --> 00:02:57.469
It is, frankly, for all of us, the opportunity of a

00:02:57.489 --> 00:02:59.279
lifetime.

00:02:59.299 --> 00:03:02.659
When I think about SEED and I think about the opportunity to

00:03:02.679 --> 00:03:06.009
really make a contribution, we want to say thank you!

00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.319
I mean we can't do it ourselves.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:12.499
But I think Stanford University can do it.

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:13.769
It's going to happen!

